This directory contains all the client certificates, CAs and CRLs used by the 'toolkit_test_server_client_expired_cert' binary.
It is used to validate the behavior of S2OPC when handling expired certificates under different scenarios:
	- Expired client certificate
	- Expired CA (root or intermediate)
	- Self-signed certificates (CA=true / CA=false depending on backend support)
	- Expired CRLs

To generate expired certificates, follow this approach:
	1. Set a very short validity period in the .cnf file (e.g. 1 day)
	2. Change your system date to the past (e.g. 2 days earlier)
	3. Generate the certificate (CA or client) using the generate_certs.sh script
	4. Restore the correct system date
→ The certificate is now considered expired and can be used for testing.

To generate expired CRLs, you can follow the same approach as for expired certificates, but use the generate_selfsigned_cert.sh instead.
